# Githooks (local)
.githooks/
# ...except the live pre-commit itself (2026-09-28): core.hooksPath points
# here, so an ignored hook is invisible enforcement. Force-tracked with
# `git add -f`; keep it that way.
!.githooks/pre-commit
nul

# Generated diagnostics (pyright/mypy dumps, session logs)
pyright_*.txt
_pyright_*.txt
_mypy_*.txt
pyright*.txt
session_log*.txt
output/
skills.win-backup/
graphify-out/

# Rust/cargo build output (regenerable)
native/*/target/
target/

# Cold store -- retired graph snapshots and oversized artifacts moved out of the
# working tree by `tools/fs_hygiene.py --kinds graph-snapshots --execute`.
# ~4.6 GB of regenerable data; must never be committed. Same reasoning as
# graphify-out/ above: it is a snapshot of the graph, not a source of truth.
var/

# Diagnostic dumps (regenerable, keep on disk)
pyright_*.txt
_pyright_*.txt
_mypy_*.txt
pyright_output.json
pyright_full*.txt
pyright_errs*.txt
pyright_now.txt
_debug_*.json
_benchmark_*.json
_e2e_*.json
_all_providers_*.json
_instruct_*.json
_eca_*.json

# Runtime evolution state — LIVE, mutated every 5 min by evolution_cycle.py.
# These must never be tracked: a git restore/checkout reverts them, which on
# 2026-09-10 silently bypassed the streak/holdout/promote/canary gates in
# reverse (production genes reverted 29.67 -> 28.23 with no promotion event).
# See EVOLUTION_PROCESS_AUDIT_20260910.md (D-1) / improvement item EV-1.
config/evolved_rl_params.json
config/evolved_rl_params.json.*
config/evolved_meta_params.json
state/evolved_rl_params.json
state/evolved_rl_params.json.*
state/evolution_pool_snapshot.json
state/evolution_pool_snapshot.json.tmp
state/holdout_cooldown.json
state/qd_archive.json
state/qd_archive.json.tmp
state/worm_policy.json
state/worm_policy.json.tmp
session_log*.txt
nul

# Runtime probe artifacts (2026-10-03): the Terence invariants oracle writes
# its own audit-trail fixtures on demand (tools/terence_invariants.py creates
# state/terence_probe_*.jsonl when absent), and chain_controller rewrites
# state/chain_controller_plan.json every cycle. Regenerable, environment
# specific, never read by a test.
state/chain_controller_plan.json
state/terence_probe_batch_audit.jsonl
state/terence_probe_empty_audit.jsonl

# Local embedding endpoint config — names a LAN LM Studio host, so it is
# machine-specific and must not be committed.
embedding_config.json

# Chunked-suite run report (tools/run_suite_chunked.py default --out). Regenerated
# every run; the summary is committed to reports/ when it matters.
logs/suite_chunks.json

# TERENCE last-run record (src/UTILITIES/TERENCE/TERENCE.py _persist_state).
# LIVE runtime state rewritten by every scan; `--status` answers
# "no-run-recorded" on a fresh checkout, which is the correct answer.
logs/terence_last_run.json

# Gray Queen entrenchment baseline — LIVE runtime state, rewritten every spine
# cycle by SpineCycleWorm._governance_stage(). The DELTA it produces is the
# whole point, so a git checkout that reverted it would report a false
# "everything is new" entrenchment spike. (Its sibling
# NEURAL_MESH_WIRE_OR_CUT.json IS tracked: that one is a reviewed declaration
# table, not telemetry.)
NEURAL_MESH_ENTRENCHMENT.json
NEURAL_MESH_ENTRENCHMENT.json.tmp

# Regenerable render output (2026-09-28): animation frames and rendered
# monitor wallboards are rebuilt by their jobs (graphify/render). Tracking
# 3,150 PPMs + wallboards meant every render dirtied the tree, so they were
# untracked (files stay on disk). dashboard/index.html stays tracked.
output/ecosystem_frames/
output/matrix_frames/
dashboard/monitor_azazael.html
dashboard/monitor_exmachina.html
dashboard/monitor_lilith.html
dashboard/monitor_ml.html
dashboard/monitor_rl.html
dashboard/command_center.html
dashboard/command_center.json

# BIBL map: the skeleton and the derived lexicon are rebuilt by
# `bibl_map.py crawl|derive|render`, so tracking them just means a 20 MB diff
# every regeneration. enrichments.json is deliberately NOT ignored -- the
# LLM-authored definitions cannot be regenerated and are the point of the map.
src/ORCHESTRATION/BIBL/skeleton.json
src/ORCHESTRATION/BIBL/enrichments.derived.json
src/ORCHESTRATION/BIBL/enrichments.merged.json
src/ORCHESTRATION/BIBL/lexicon/
# Superseded WORMZ output, kept on disk as the only surviving record of a
# format nothing can now generate. Not source; see _spec_snapshot_20260929/
# for the Kali copy that is worth keeping.
src/ORCHESTRATION/BIBL/archive/

# MorphogenesisWorm staging output (2026-10-02). Every file under here is
# auto-generated ("do not edit by hand"), non-autonomous -- execute() only
# records evidence -- and named `gen_<worm>_<unknown|nature>.py`. The migration
# ledger quarantined the 91-file set (`keep iff a unit claims a file`) and no
# unit does, so they are excluded rather than adopted. `pyrightconfig.json`
# already excludes the same glob; this stops them entering `git status` as
# invisible work as well. Delete this line only alongside a claim on a file.
src/CORE/WORMS/expansion/generated/_staging/
